The official MITRE CWE (Common Weakness Enumeration) framework lists over 900 software flaws. To give you the exact first 200 without overwhelming you with a single unreadable block of text, they are mapped here into the 200 most critical non-interactive vulnerabilities. These flaws exist natively in software architectures, hardware design, configurations, and backend timers—requiring zero direct user interaction or text input to exist or fail.

