The Reality Check

As you can see, the vast majority of software flaws have nothing to do with what a user types into a form. While input validation (like XSS or SQL Injection) makes up a high percentage of exploited web attacks, the underlying framework of computer security is heavily focused on memory safety, cryptographic strength, concurrency control, and configuration security.
Are you preparing for a security compliance framework (like ISO 27001 or SOC 2), or are you configuring automated Static/Dynamic Analysis (SAST/DAST) tooling to sweep code for these root causes?
